{#
  The ML-DSA identity trustpoint, enrolled by hand against an offline CA.

  /native/crypto/pki/trustpoint[id]/enrollment/enrollment-method/terminal/pem
  /native/crypto/pki/trustpoint[id]/subject-name
  /native/crypto/pki/trustpoint[id]/revocation-check
  /native/crypto/pki/trustpoint[id]/hash
  /native/crypto/pki/trustpoint[id]/fingerprint
  /native/crypto/pki/trustpoint[id]/mldsakeypair/{key-label,parameter-set}

  Separate from roles/common/templates/pki-trustpoint.xml.j2, which is the SCEP
  shape used by the EAP-TLS unit. The difference is the whole point of this role:
  enrollment-method is a YANG choice, and this one takes terminal-case rather than
  url-case, so there is no CA URL, no SCEP and no CMS envelope anywhere in it.

  The "pem" leaf under terminal is worth having. Without it IOS brackets the
  request with its own prose banners ("Certificate Request follows:" and
  "---End - This line not part of the certificate request---") and emits bare
  base64; with it you get real -----BEGIN CERTIFICATE REQUEST----- boundaries,
  which is one less thing for the parser to get wrong.

  mldsakeypair is the 26.2 addition: leaf key-label plus leaf parameter-set, whose
  YANG range is literally "44 | 65 | 87". The key itself is generated on the box
  beforehand in exec mode; this only binds the trustpoint to that label. Note that
  the CLI behind this node does not parse without "service internal", which the
  role turns on first and puts back afterwards.

  fingerprint pins the CA certificate by its MD5, computed on the control node
  from the DER form. Pinning it is not tidiness: without it "crypto pki
  authenticate" stops and asks "% Do you accept this certificate? [yes/no]:", and
  answering a yes/no blind is the one thing this layer never does.

  revocation-check none is a lab answer. The trustpoint default is crl, and this
  CA publishes no CRL distribution point, so the router would go looking for a CRL
  it can never find and stall IKE_AUTH.
-#}
<config xmlns="urn:ietf:params:xml:ns:netconf:base:1.0"
        xmlns:nc="urn:ietf:params:xml:ns:netconf:base:1.0">
  <native xmlns="http://cisco.com/ns/yang/Cisco-IOS-XE-native">
    <crypto>
      <pki xmlns="http://cisco.com/ns/yang/Cisco-IOS-XE-crypto">
        <trustpoint>
          <id>{{ pki_names.mldsa_trustpoint }}</id>
          <enrollment>
            <enrollment-method>
              <terminal>
                <pem/>
              </terminal>
            </enrollment-method>
          </enrollment>
          <subject-name>{{ mldsa_subject_name }}</subject-name>
          <revocation-check>{{ pki_revocation_check }}</revocation-check>
          <hash>{{ pki_hash }}</hash>
          <fingerprint>{{ mldsa_ca_fingerprint }}</fingerprint>
          <mldsakeypair>
            <key-label>{{ pki_names.mldsa_key_label }}</key-label>
            <parameter-set>{{ pq_signature_param_set }}</parameter-set>
          </mldsakeypair>
        </trustpoint>
      </pki>
    </crypto>
  </native>
</config>
